# Ownership layering (doc 08 §1). Paths are relative to this file's directory;
# in the CI harness (fm-pipeline-ci) this file sits at the repo root and is live.
#
# Humans own the spec layer: domain contract, properties, snapshots, gate config.
# The LLM owns the implementation file and iterates against gate feedback.
#
# NOTE (tested, Unit 10): on a solo account, require_code_owner_reviews cannot be
# satisfied (self-review does not count), so enforcement is via the required
# status check `pr-gate`; this file remains the review-request signal.

# Default: everything requests owner review
* @kasa

# Human-owned spec layer (explicit, for visibility even though `*` covers it)
/spec/                        @kasa
/PipelineTests/Properties.cs  @kasa
/PipelineTests/Snapshots.cs   @kasa
/PipelineTests/ArchitectureTests.cs @kasa
**/*.verified.txt             @kasa
**/*.received.*               @kasa
/Directory.Build.props        @kasa
/**/*.csproj                  @kasa
/stryker-config.json          @kasa
/.config/dotnet-tools.json    @kasa
/scripts/                     @kasa
/gates/                       @kasa
/.github/workflows/           @kasa
/CODEOWNERS                   @kasa

# LLM-owned implementation (subject to every gate; matches `*` above for review):
# /src/DiscountPolicy/DiscountPolicy.cs
